WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.120
On your way to retrieve the Lotus of the Palace,

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.440
you journey through the Sunken Valley, a place that's inaccessible to most.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.340
In it coils a white serpent, an old god of the land.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:16.480
It's worshipped by the Sunken Valley Clan, a forlorn people who man the Gunfort.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.440
Deeper still, you'll find the valley where the monkeys dwell,

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.060
where the Sculptor trained to become a shinobi.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.660
He trained with a partner here, named Kingfisher,

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.180
a woman who would go on to be consumed by an undying ape.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.020
The lore runs deep here.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.540
Let's talk about it.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.820
This is the Great Serpent.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.740
A god of the land, or so the Sunken Valley Clan believe.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.600
They don't just worship the snake;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.180
rather, they worship the heart,

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.700
for the heart is believed to be where one's spirit resides.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.660
They enshrine the organs,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.800
believing that they represent the deity itself,

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.520
and with two hearts

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.360
you can initiate the Dragon's Return ending,

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:05.800
an ending that has the Divine Child of the Rejuvenating Waters become a cradle for the Dragon's Blood,

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.500
which allows the Sakura Dragon to leave Japan.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.740
For when the Sakura Dragon came from the West and took root in Ashina,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.940
many lesser gods left,

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:19.420
and the Serpent God was almost certainly one of them.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.240
Look ahead to Mibu Village for proof.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.500
Here, we find scraps of snake skin

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.820
caught upon rooftops and dangling from the gates,

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:32.920
and it may not have just been the Serpent God that left this place;

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:37.760
Buddha, too, has been desecrated here as a result of the Sakura Dragon.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.180
Furthermore,

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.640
just as snake statues are found all throughout Senpou Temple,

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:47.900
so too are Buddha statues found within the Sunken Valley,

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.560
home of the Serpent God.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:55.800
These statues seem like they were intended to hold the two hearts of the Great Serpents.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.220
The first statue is cradling a snake skin,

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.820
which likely belonged to the full-grown snake just beyond.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.900
The second heart, however, lies in a cave.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.660
Toxic Memorial Mob: "You there.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:11.460
Don't go into that cave up ahead.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:17.420
Inside is an old shrine, where the Serpent God dwells,

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:20.920
and if the Serpent God swallows you...

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:25.540
...you can't buy any more offerings, now, can you?"

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.640
This dried heart might have belonged to an older serpent,

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:33.840
a spirit that was passed from Buddha's hands to ours,

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.360
so that we can pursue the Dragon's Return.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:37.520
Food for thought.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:41.180
So, those are the Serpent God's hearts,

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.340
but what about its eyes?

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:46.280
The Snake Eyes are the commanders of the Sunken Valley Clan,

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:50.920
female fighters equipped with flint cannons and blessed with phenomenal vision.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.980
As the Eyes of the Snake,

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.700
they've positioned themselves at both entrances to the Sunken Valley,

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:00.340
striking fear into any stranger who approaches,

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:03.060
and not only do they watch out for the snake,

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.820
those of the Sunken Valley also offer themselves to it in "marriage".

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:12.780
Well, "marriage" in quotation marks, because it really means "to make an offering of oneself",

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.960
such is their devotion to the Serpent God.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.100
But when they're not feeding themselves to a snake,

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:23.360
it's likely that the Sunken Valley Clan is busy mining the precious metals of the Valley.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.580
Magnetic deposits are found all over the Valley,

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.700
and their value is evident,

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:35.340
for the Sunken Valley Clan ended up concocting medicines to help them resist the toxic state of this place,

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:41.200
and while it's said that those who stay here long enough can overcome their weakness to poison,

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.380
two prominent women here are still devastated by it.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.660
These are the Snake Eyes,

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:47.860
commanders of the clan,

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:53.300
and they are no match for Sabimaru, your poisonous prosthetic kodachi blade,

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.340
and there's a reason for this,

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:56.580
for the blade reads,

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.440
"Sabimaru was wielded in wars of old,

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.980
and is a national treasure of Ashina.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:06.980
It was once used to drive off the inhuman Okami warrior women,

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.860
and even now, it is likely to be effective against their descendants."

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.280
The Snake Eyes are descendants of the ancient Okami Clan.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:17.800
"Okami" means "Dragon",

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:23.280
and it's likely referring to the clan of carp-like beings that you find in Fountainhead Palace,

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.840
because long, long ago,

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.340
in the most ancient days of the Ashina,

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:32.020
this Okami Clan gathered the Fountainhead Fragrance

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.440
and arrived at the Palace.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.840
They pledged themselves to the Sakura Serpent,

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.540
making ceremonial blood offerings to it,

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:44.240
which is an act that is not unlike what the Sunken Valley Clan did.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.660
They, too, offer themselves in "marriage" to the Serpent God;

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:54.600
the difference is while one Clan dances joyously in a Divine Realm,

00:04:54.600 --> 00:05:00.640
the other Clan sits sullenly atop the frozen, poisonous cliff face of the Sunken Valley.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:07.180
One incredibly neat detail is that the Okami warrior women are master marksmen;

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:12.180
they have this godlike accuracy with the bow, lightning bolt and...

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:12.840
...soccer ball?

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:19.200
Just so, their descendants, too, can also hit their targets from half a league away,

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:23.200
still using ranged weapons just like their ancestors,

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:27.400
except now ones that have been adapted for the modern age.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:31.260
There are some benefits to being left behind, it seems,

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.280
and that's a point of contention:

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.960
whether they were left behind or not,

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:41.160
and it's something I've found myself going back and forth on the entire time I've been scripting this.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.860
There are two options that I see,

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.835
and the question is this:

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:51.100
was the Sunken Valley Clan left behind when the rest of their Clan ascended,

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.240
staying loyal to the Serpent God

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.640
whereas the Okami went on to worship the Sakura Dragon?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.600
Or did the Okami ascend to the Divine Realm

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:02.600
and then return,

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.920
with some serpent-worshipping descendants

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:08.220
going on to settle in the Sunken Valley?

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:16.500
And make no mistake: the Okami Clan did eventually come back - that is a fact - after they ascended to the Divine Realm.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:19.540
They brought the thunder with them,

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.140
invading Ashina and killing its people.

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.280
The game calls this "an old war";

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:28.520
it's a long-forgotten event, so

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:30.980
it's no surprise that the details are scarce.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.680
We don't even know why they invaded.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.720
I'm curious to hear your thoughts.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:40.200
But what we do know is that the Okami were eventually repelled

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.660
by Sabimaru,

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:43.860
an heirloom forged by the Ashina.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:48.680
This weapon held the poisonous gift of blue rust,

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:51.180
which was Kryptonite to the Okami warriors.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:56.280
The context of this war changes, dependent on whether you believe that

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:00.120
the Sunken Valley Clan was left behind when the Okami ascended,

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:04.320
or whether you believe that the Sunken Valley Clan came to exist

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:08.480
after the Okami invaded, and descended from the Fountainhead.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:10.920
There's evidence for both ideas;

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:16.100
I can't find one piece of evidence that makes it true beyond reason,

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:20.340
so, I'll tell you both stories, and you can decide what to believe.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.540
So first,

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:25.340
the Sunken Valley Clan may have come to exist as a result

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.280
of the Okamis' failed invasion.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:31.620
The Green Mossy Gourd says that it was "made out of necessity

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:34.840
by those who made poisonous lands their home."

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:39.560
It's said that if you live there long enough, eventually poison won't affect you at all.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:45.380
If the Okami were indeed bitter at being defeated by poison,

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:49.540
then perhaps they wished to overcome this weakness over generations of exposure.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:56.380
Alternatively, it's also fair to believe that the Sunken Valley Clan was left behind by the Okami Clan

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.540
when they ascended to the Divine Realm.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:03.580
If this was the case, then they would have learned about their weakness to poison

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.760
from living in the Valley all this time,

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:09.860
and they may have helped the Ashina forge Sabimaru

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:12.715
when the Okami came back and invaded.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:17.440
Sabimaru was "gifted" with poisonous blue rust, after all,

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:22.840
and there is evidence of an alliance between the Sunken Valley Clan and Ashina;

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:26.440
many of the Sunken Valley man the watchtowers of the Ashina,

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:32.660
and the key to their Gunfort Shrine is  even kept in the private quarters of the Ashina Elite.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:39.200
Together, the Ashina and the Sunken Valley Clan may well have repelled the inhuman Okami.

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:40.500
I like this theory more.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.200
The Ashina called the Okami Clan "inhuman"

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.940
and while you would assume that that means that they

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:50.500
invaded in their carp-like state,

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.160
they may not have,

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:55.100
for Sabimaru calls them "spirits",

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:58.620
and this scroll of an old battle calls them "ghosts".

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.600
"Ghosts once lurked the lands of Ashina.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:04.840
The Ghosts' lightning was of the Fountainhead gods,

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:06.580
unstoppable by normal means."

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:12.120
Whatever the case, the ancient Ashina were besieged by their lightning,

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:16.040
and so, in addition to Sabimaru, which was an offensive tool,

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:19.040
they actually developed a few measures as well.

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:22.380
First was the Art of Lightning Reversal,

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:26.620
and there's a guide to how to perform it hung in their dojo

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:28.240
where their warriors train,

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:31.620
and second was something called "Eel Livers".

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:34.180
Eels are relatives of dragons,

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:37.700
and they allowed the Ashina to suppress the lightning,

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:39.000
the force of the gods.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.800
Though admittedly, this didn't work for very long.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:45.240
This drug is littered throughout Ashina Castle,

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.900
and they even offered it ceremoniously

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.140
at a couple of shrines.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:53.300
It's this remnant of an ancient war against the Okami.

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:57.060
It's no surprise then that, given all of this,

00:09:57.060 --> 00:10:01.560
the Ashina did come to consider lightning powers as "heretical":

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:03.880
Genichiro names them as such,

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:06.720
when he invokes the name of his master, Tomoe.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.700
Genichiro: "I will seize any manner of heretical strength."

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:13.820
Tomoe was also of the Okami;

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:16.600
she descended via the "Floating Passage",

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:19.180
and she was this benevolent being who

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.180
decided to live amongst the Ashina.

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.440
Reflective of her Clan,

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:26.420
she likely taught Genichiro how to use that bow of his,

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:30.020
and she also taught him the Lightning Arts that

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:32.120
he would go to practice fervently.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:34.900
She would eventually sacrifice everything

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.740
for a boy named Takeru,

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.320
a boy cursed with the Dragon's Heritage,

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.680
but that story Is one for another time.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:46.020
We follow the notes that Tomoe and Takeru left us,

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:48.080
and they, in turn,

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:51.400
are following the knowledge that was left by Tomoe's relatives,

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:54.680
the Okami clan, when they first ascended to the Divine Realm.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:58.680
This is knowledge that guides us towards the Fountainhead Fragrance,

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:02.620
which requires us to obtain the Lotus of the Palace,

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:06.220
which grows where the Fountainhead Waters pool deeply.

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:11.140
On our way to said Lotus, we travel through the Bodhisattva Valley,

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:13.240
the place where the monkeys dwell,

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:19.720
and fruits hidden by monkeys in tree hollows can sometimes ferment and turn into sake,

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:20.720
with a bit of luck.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.380
Sculptor: *drinks, coughs* "It burns the throat, same as ever.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.760
This really brings back memories.

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:32.500
I trained in the techniques of the Shinobi, in the Valley where the monkeys dwelled..."

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:33.840
Sekiro: "By yourself?"

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:35.100
Sculptor: "...No.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:36.620
There were two of us.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.820
We were rogue Shinobi...

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:41.300
...there was no proper master for the likes of us.

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:44.320
That's why we went to the Valley:

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:47.220
to run, to jump, to clash swords...

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.420
...where one slip would mean your doom.

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:51.420
That was how we trained.

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:56.260
We came to move exactly as monkeys did after a time... *drinks*

00:11:56.760 --> 00:12:02.000
I drank this Monkey Booze whenever I tired of training,

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:07.440
and I'd listen to the howl of my partner's whistling finger while I drank.

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:13.340
Whistling through that ring would fill the Valley with a somber melody.

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:18.500
Strangely enough, I enjoyed that sound..."

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:22.040
The Sculptor's partner was called Kingfisher,

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:23.940
the name that was etched onto her ring.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:28.960
Her cry could once be heard all along the waterfront of the Sunken Valley,

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:32.120
and her whistle could be used to drive beasts wild.

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:33.900
Speaking of which...

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:36.040
This is the Guardian Ape,

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.660
sitting in the cove where the Fountainhead Waters pool.

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:42.880
It's cultivating this Lotus to give to its mate,

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:45.880
for the Ape actually lost his previous partner,

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:48.600
whose corpse you find hidden away in an alcove.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:52.520
It's been so long since he lost her, though,

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:56.000
that even the flowers offered in tribute to her passing

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.160
have withered to dust.

00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:59.520
For the Ape is immortal;

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:04.560
this is thanks to the Centipede, which emerges when you sever the Ape's head

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:07.900
using this gigantic sword that

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:11.980
likely once belonged to the Sculptor's training partner, the Kingfisher.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:15.200
It's an incredible weapon, but it's no Mortal Blade,

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:19.560
and within the immortal Ape's belly, we find the Kingfisher's ring.

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:21.780
Sculptor: "What's that you have there?

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:23.900
Where did you get that finger?"

00:13:24.225 --> 00:13:26.395
Sekiro: "The Guardian Ape of the Sunken Valley.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:28.700
I found it in his belly."

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:30.460
Sculptor: "I see...

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:32.900
...to think it was in the belly of an ape...

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:37.220
...I'm sure it will play a somber, but enjoyable tune.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.340
Make sure you use it well."

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:43.100
If she is indeed dead,

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:47.360
then the loss of this woman could have been what first led

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:49.540
the Sculptor to become Shura,

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:53.460
for when the Sculptor turns again at the end of the game,

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:56.840
you can use the Kingfisher's ring to play a somber tune.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:00.600
A weeping voice, full of solitude and beauty,

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:03.900
somber enough to temporarily quell a voice of rage.

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:13.420
With the Kingfisher avenged, we can claim the Lotus of the Palace,

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:17.420
putting us one step closer to the Fountainhead Fragrance.

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:20.800
Next, we travel to Ashina Depths,

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:22.560
to this bottomless hole,

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:24.240
to the Hidden Forest,

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:25.420
and to Mibu Village.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:30.340
Remember to hit the notification bell, so you don't miss when the video goes live,

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:31.500
and I'll see you next time.

